-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Licensing statement
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DeepMap is MIT-licensed. It runs on a local Neo4j Community Edition instance
(GPLv3), which DeepMap downloads from the official source but does not
redistribute or modify, and accesses over the standard Bolt protocol. DeepMap's
own MIT-licensed code is independent of Neo4j's license. If you use DeepMap
commercially, review Neo4j's licensing terms (or consult counsel) for your use
of Neo4j Community.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prerequisite (FETCHED at install time — NOT bundled or redistributed)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Neo4j Community Edition (5.x; the provisioner fetches 5.26.32 by default;
    a store created with an earlier 5.26 release keeps it until setup moves it
    to 5.26.32) — GPLv3
    (its source headers grant version 3 "or, at your option, any later version")
    Downloaded from the official source (dist.neo4j.org) by setup; accessed
    arms-length over the Bolt network protocol. Not bundled and not
    redistributed, and its code is not modified (setup writes only DeepMap's own
    settings into neo4j.conf on the user's machine, including switching off
    Neo4j's usage reporting). Listed here as a prerequisite, not as a bundled
    component, so DeepMap's MIT code is not subject to the GPLv3 combined-work
    obligation.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Python dependencies (installed from PyPI, not redistributed)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Three of these are PINNED to the version ranges they were validated on — the
same ranges as requirements.txt, both installers and CI, each installed with
`pip install --upgrade` so an older copy is lifted into the range:
neo4j>=6.0.1,<7 · mcp>=1.24,<2 · graphifyy>=0.8.39,<0.8.52. The others stay
unpinned (no known breaking release), except that anyio is declared with mcp's
own floor (below).

* Upstream multi-language extraction engine — "graphify" / "graphifyy"
    (Graphify-Labs/graphify, formerly safishamsi/graphify) — MIT for every
    release DeepMap's pin allows (<0.8.52). Upstream relicensed to Apache-2.0
    from 0.9.25 (2026-07-22): re-check this attribution before widening the pin.
    SHIPPED and used unchanged: the multi-language extractor (DEEPMAP_EXTRACTOR=
    graphify|auto), installed BARE (no extras) by both installers +
    requirements.txt with
      pip install --upgrade "graphifyy>=0.8.39,<0.8.52"
    Validated at 0.8.39 and 0.8.51 (the releases between were diffed
    statically); 0.8.52+ and 0.9.x are outside the validated range. Its optional
    LLM-provider extras (openai/anthropic/bedrock/…) are deliberately NOT
    installed, so a default install ships NO LLM SDK; DeepMap invokes only
    `graphify update --no-cluster` (NO LLM, NO clustering, NO network) —
    zero-egress by construction. The PyPI package is `graphifyy`; its import
    name, `graphify`, is used unchanged. This MIT attribution is retained.
* sentence-transformers — Apache-2.0 (includes an express patent grant)
* transformers — Apache-2.0
* torch (CPU build) — BSD-3-Clause
* neo4j (Python Bolt driver) — Apache-2.0 AND Python-2.0 (its PyPI license
    expression) — pinned neo4j>=6.0.1,<7 (validated at
    6.0.1, 6.2.0 and 6.3.1)
* mcp (MCP Python SDK) — MIT — pinned mcp>=1.24,<2 (validated at 1.24.0, 1.28.1
    and 1.30.0); both MCP servers `from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP`
* anyio (agronholm/anyio) — MIT — declared anyio>=4.5 in requirements.txt,
    mcp's own floor, no ceiling (no known breaking release). It arrives with
    mcp, and DeepMap also imports it directly: the MCP servers run each tool
    body in a worker thread under a deadline (build/mcp_bounds.py) and bound
    the search server's project-guard roots request
    (build/deepmap_search_server.py). Both installers install it next to mcp
    with the same floor; CI gets it through mcp.
* huggingface_hub — Apache-2.0 (pre-downloads the embedding model via snapshot_download)
* PyYAML — MIT (parses the benchmark's repos.yaml / questions.yaml; the harness also carries a stdlib
    fallback, but both installers pip-install it, so it is attributed here)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model weights (FETCHED at install time — not bundled: about 0.6 GB, because
/deep-map:setup and both installers skip the ONNX / OpenVINO exports)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* nomic-ai/modernbert-embed-base — Apache-2.0
    A GENERAL-TEXT embedding model (768-dim). DeepMap embeds structural intent
    summaries with it (a symbol's docstring line, else a deterministic
    name/params/callees synthesis — see build/summarize.py; no LLM call); it is
    NOT a "code-trained" model.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not dependencies (listed for the record)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* ranx — MIT — NOT A DEPENDENCY
    Fusion is implemented directly in a pure-Python `_weighted_rrf`
    (build/retrieval.py); nothing in DeepMap imports ranx, and neither
    requirements.txt nor the installers (install.sh / install.ps1) install it.
* mcp-neo4j-cypher (neo4j-contrib/mcp-neo4j) — MIT — NOT shipped and not a
    dependency: DeepMap's read-only Cypher tool (deepmap_cypher) is its own
    code. Neo4j's official MCP server (neo4j/mcp) is GPL-3.0 and is likewise
    not shipped.
* APOC (Core) — Apache-2.0 — NOT USED: DeepMap neither fetches, enables nor
    calls APOC. The Neo4j distribution carries a disabled
    labs/apoc-*-core.jar; DeepMap leaves it disabled.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- The only copyleft component DeepMap depends on directly is Neo4j Community
  (GPLv3), fetched-not-bundled (above).
- All other direct dependencies are permissive (MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD-3).
  No AGPL.
- DeepMap is local-only, zero-telemetry: no SaaS/network-copyleft question arises.
  (Neo4j Community sends a usage report by default; setup switches it off in
  every instance it provisions. A Neo4j you point DeepMap at yourself, through
  NEO4J_URI, keeps its own settings.)
- A machine-readable SBOM is provided in sbom.cdx.json (CycloneDX). It is a
  hand-maintained SEED: neo4j, mcp and graphifyy carry the validated ranges above
  and anyio its declared floor (tests/compliance_gates.py keeps them equal to
  requirements.txt), the other components are unpinned; regenerate it from the
  installed environment for exact versions.
